      { "reader": "Bryn", "kind": "said", "words": "Junction" },
      { "reader": "Bryn", "kind": "said", "words": "You are at the junction of a north-south passage and an east-west passage. To the north, you can make out the bottom of a stairway. The ways to the east and south are relatively cramped, but a wider trail leads to the west." },
      { "reader": "Bryn", "kind": "said", "words": "Standing before you is a great rock. Imbedded within it is an Elvish sword." }
    ] },
