    { "as": "Bryn", "type": "examine figure", "expect": [
      { "reader": "Bryn", "kind": "described", "words": "A figure in a hood and a cloak, both dark, both plain, standing the way you stand and holding its sword the way you hold yours, which you had not noticed you did until now. The hood casts a shadow where a face should be, and the sword glows with the same cold blue light as your own. It is watching you; you can feel it watching you, as you can feel yourself watching it." },
      { "reader": "Bryn", "kind": "described", "words": "The hooded figure appears to be badly hurt and defenseless." },
      { "reader": "Bryn", "kind": "described", "words": "It has stopped fighting the way you fight; it has stopped fighting at all. It stands with the point of its sword in the ground and its head bowed, and the hood, which has kept its face from you all this while, hangs within reach of your hand." },
      { "reader": "Bryn", "kind": "told", "words": "The hooded figure attempts a thrust, but its weakened state prevents hitting you." }
    ] },
